    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0524" n="512" xml:id="pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">381.81/320a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Acting American Representative to the French Committee of National
                        Liberation at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chapin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-12T20:00:00-04:00">February 12,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>470. Reference Casablanca’s telegram no. 32, February 4, 5 p.m. Please submit a
                    full report at once, on reported action of Combined Food Committee at Algiers in
                    insisting that French authorities requisition entire olive crop of persons under
                    American protection in French Morocco. The Department would take a serious view
                    of any attempt to infringe the treaty rights of American <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ressortissants</hi> in Morocco. The Department has emphasized repeatedly
                    that no decrees promulgated in Morocco are applicable to American protégés until
                    this Government’s consent is conveyed to the Resident General.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Casablanca.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
